  "body": "Version 1.26.4 of ART (commit 71e0bde9356b259478d6e99c002f18f311d6c671) added an awesome new feature: it added this new button in the \"Editor\" mode\n<img width=\"502\" height=\"176\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/67ba0a36-e856-4197-9158-754275ac5347\" />\n\nHowever, when this feature is enabled, I encounter an issue when I try to create an area mask for local editing, following the instructions found on this page: https://artraweditor.github.io/Shapes.html\n\nCreating a shape by adding points with Ctrl + click works correctly. However, once points and lines are drawn, it's impossible to select and manipulate them with the mouse. The points and lines between them are supposed to turn orange when you hover them with the mouse pointer, but it just doesn't happen. Clicking has no effect. Clicking + dragging just moves the view.\n\nSimilarly, gradients and rectangular shapes can't be modified either.\n\nThis functionality is restored when I disable \"pixel-for-pixel\" mode by clicking again on the button I mentioned in the beginning.\n\n### Environment\nWindows 11 25H2 build 26200.8457\nART 1.26.4\nASUS laptop with screen resolution 3200x2000\nGlobal scaling in Windows' screen settings: 200%\n\nI can provide some more details if you find that the issue is not reproducible on your side.",
